id: 27
hanzi: 守岁
pinyin: shǒu suì
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to stay up late on New Year's Eve; to see the old year out and the new year in
  es: pasar la nochevieja en vela; velar el año nuevo; trasnochar en vísperas de año nuevo

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to stay awake through the night on Lunar New Year's Eve with family to usher in the new year | pasar la nochevieja en vela junto a la familia para despedir el año viejo y recibir el nuevo | 全家守岁 (the whole family stays up for New Year's Eve)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 除夕之夜，全家人围坐在明亮的客厅里一边包饺子看春晚，一边欢笑着守岁到天明。 | Chúxī zhī yè, quánjiā rén wéizuò zài míngliàng de kètīng lǐ yìbiān bāo jiǎozi kàn chūnwǎn, yìbiān huānxiào zhe shǒusuì dào tiānmíng. | On New Year's Eve, the entire family gathered in the brightly lit living room, making dumplings and watching the gala while laughing and staying up late to welcome the dawn. | En nochevieja, la familia al completo se reunió en la sala iluminada preparando empanadillas y viendo la gala, charlando alegremente hasta el alba para recibir el nuevo año.
  #2 | 民俗学者指出，除夕守岁的古老仪式不仅象征着对流逝光阴的深切眷恋，更寄托了为长辈祈求健康长寿的美好愿望。 | Mínsú xuézhě zhǐchū, Chúxī shǒusuì de gǔlǎo yíshì bùjǐn xiàngzhēng zhe duì liúshì guāngyīn de shēnqiè juànliàn, gèng jìtuō le wèi zhǎngbèi qíqiú jiànkāng chángshòu de měihǎo yuànwàng. | Folklorists point out that the ancient ritual of staying up late on New Year's Eve not only symbolizes deep attachment to passing time, but also embodies hopes of praying for elders' health and longevity. | Los antropólogos destacan que la costumbre de velar en fin de año simboliza el apego al tiempo ido y encarna el devoto deseo de salud y longevidad para los mayores.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  全家守岁 | the whole family stays up late on New Year's Eve
  守岁习俗 | the custom of staying up late on New Year's Eve
  一起守岁 | stay up late together on New Year's Eve
  除夕守岁 | stay up late on New Year's Eve
  围炉守岁 | sit around the hearth staying up for the new year
  守岁到天明 | stay up late until dawn

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  岁岁平安 | suì suì píng ān | peace and safety year after year
  岁寒知松柏 | suì hán zhī sōng bǎi | only in the cold of winter does one know the resilience of pine and cypress
  恪尽职守 | kè jìn zhí shǒu | conscientiously fulfill one's duties
  守望相助 | shǒu wàng xiāng zhù | keep watch and help one another; mutual surveillance and assistance

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  守 | shǒu | guard; protect; watch; observe | guardar; custodiar; vigilar; proteger | 宀 | roof / house | 宀 (roof / home) | 寸 (cùn, inch / hand / rule) | 6 | 上下结构 | Ideogrammic compound of roof (宀) guarded by a watchful hand or law (寸), signifying defending one's household and rules. | A vigilant hand (寸) held ready under the household roof (宀) to protect the sanctuary of home. | Una mano protectora (寸) atenta bajo el techo del hogar (宀) custodiando la paz de la casa. | 214 | JDI | ""
  岁 | suì | year; age; harvest | año; edad; cosecha; tiempo | 山 | mountain | 山 (mountain / passage of years) | 夕 (evening / moon phases) | 6 | 上下结构 | Simplified from traditional 歲 (which combined 步 step with 戌 battle axe / planetary orbit). Modern form joins 山 and 夕, evoking seasons passing over mountains. | Evening moons (夕) setting over jagged mountain peaks (山) marking the turning of another full year. | La luna vespertina (夕) que cae tras las cumbres montañosas (山) señalando el giro de un nuevo año. | 51 | UMNI | 歲

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Guarding the house (守) as the old year turns (岁) keeps the family vigil of 'shǒusuì' alive.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Custodiar el hogar (守) mientras gira el año (岁) da vida a la vigilia tradicional de nochevieja (守岁).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: The tradition of 守岁 dates back to the Northern and Southern Dynasties (recorded in Jingchu Suishiji). For elders, it means 'cherishing passing time' (惜光阴); for youths, it means praying for their parents' longevity (延年益寿). In folklore, it commemorates staying awake to avoid being ambushed by the monster Nian.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipped 3rd tone 'shǒu' (214) followed by falling 4th tone 'suì' (51). Ensure 'shǒu' dips to low pitch 1 before cleanly launching into 'suì'.

