semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 守岁 specifically denotes the cultural custom of staying awake all night on Lunar New Year's Eve to bid farewell to the old year and welcome the new.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 守岁 vs. 熬夜 | áoyè | 守岁 is a joyful, festive ritual steeped in filial devotion and cultural celebration on New Year's Eve, whereas 熬夜 is a mundane, exhausting act of working or staying up late on any ordinary night.
    2 | 守岁 vs. 过年 | guònián | 守岁 refers strictly to the vigil during the single night of New Year's Eve, whereas 过年 encompasses the broad weeks-long celebration of the entire Spring Festival season.
    3 | 守岁 vs. 拜年 | bàinián | 守岁 takes place overnight indoors on New Year's Eve among immediate family, whereas 拜年 involves visiting relatives and friends to extend New Year greetings starting on New Year's Day morning.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 除夕夜的灯火彻夜通明，全家老小围坐桌旁守岁。长辈眷恋岁月的沉淀，晚辈祈盼父母健康长寿。守岁不仅守住了一份浓郁年味，更凝聚着生生不息的家族深情。 | Chúxī yè de dēnghuǒ chèyè tōngmíng, quánjiā lǎoxiǎo wéizuò zhuō páng shǒusuì. Zhǎngbèi juànliàn suìyuè de chéndiàn, wǎnbèi qípàn fùmǔ jiànkāng chángshòu. Shǒusuì bùjǐn shǒuzhù le yí fèn nóngyù niánwèi, gèng níngjù zhe shēngshēng-bùxī de jiāzú shēnqíng. | The lights on New Year's Eve shone bright all through the night as young and old sat together staying up late. Elders cherished the accumulation of years while the young prayed for their parents' health and longevity. Staying up late not only guards festive sentiment, but knits enduring family bonds. | Las luces de fin de año resplandecieron toda la noche mientras la familia velaba unida. Los mayores evocaron el paso del tiempo y los jóvenes oraron por su salud y larga vida. Velar en nochevieja salvaguarda el espíritu festivo y consolida el afecto familiar intergeneracional.
  #2 | 随着现代都市生活节奏加快，传统守岁的仪式形态虽在悄然改变，但其团聚内核依然坚固。无论是线上互道祝福还是全家通宵促膝长谈，守岁习俗始终是维系中华民族精神凝聚力与家国情怀的重要文化纽带。 | Suízhe xiàndài dūshì shēnghuó jiézòu jiākuài, chuántǒng shǒusuì de yíshì xíngtài suī zài qiǎorán gǎibiàn, dàn qí tuánjù nèihé yīrán jiāngù. Wúlùn shì xiànshàng hùdào zhùfú háishì quánjiā tōngxiāo cùxī-chángtán, shǒusuì xísú shǐzhōng shì wéixì Zhōnghuá mínzú jīngshén níngjùlì yǔ jiāguó qínghuái de zhòngyào wénhuà niǔdài. | As the tempo of contemporary urban life quickens, although outer forms of the New Year's vigil are evolving, its reunion core remains steadfast. Whether exchanging greetings online or chatting face-to-face all night, the custom of staying up late serves as an essential cultural bond sustaining Chinese cohesion and familial devotion. | Aunque la vida urbana moderna transforma las formas externas de velar el año nuevo, su esencia de reunión comunitaria perdura intacta. Ya sea felicitándose en red o conversando hasta el amanecer, esta vigilia sigue siendo un lazo cultural indispensable que afianza la cohesión del pueblo chino.